 "relevance_note": "Narrative review of autoinflammatory bone diseases that describes one of the authors' own patients with Majeed syndrome: \"An 8-year-old male patient who presented to us with leg pain was diagnosed with Majeed syndrome\".",
 "method_note": "Built by hand with a short script; every value read from the paper. The paper is a review; the only in-scope person is the authors' own 8-year-old boy with Majeed syndrome (Majeed syndrome section, Figure 3g). Other own patients (CNO, SAPHO, cherubism) are out of scope. Label 'unnamed person 1' (rule 6: not a case report, no own label; counted among in-scope people only). No LPIN2 variant or genetic testing is reported for him (diagnosis stated as following an MRI), so no variant row was created. The age '8-year-old' is his age when he presented and was diagnosed; recorded as age at diagnosis. 'Leg pain' recorded as a feature only; it was not mapped to the checklist items 'bone pain' or 'joint pain', and CRMO was not marked because the MRI findings are only in Figure 3g, not described in text. General disease descriptions in the review (CDA, Sweet syndrome, fever, neutropenia, etc.) are not about this patient and were not used. No previously published individuals are described with individual-level detail. No contradictions found.",
